title: IslandQuestDeniz
---

DENIZ: (head snaps towards SASHA, followed by a long sigh)
DENIZ: (irritated) “What did they do now?”


-> “No, no. Nothing at all.. I just wanted to know.”
	SASHA: “No, no. Nothing at all.. I just wanted to know.”
	DENIZ: (nods, looks back at the water)
	<<stop>>
-> “Can you tell me a bit about them?”
	SASHA: “Can you tell me a bit about them?”
	DENIZ: (presses lips in a fine line, then sighs) What do you want to know, then?
	
<<jump DenizQuests>>

===
title: DenizQuests
---

-> “What’s their.. work?” <<if $DenizAnger1 == false>>
	SASHA: “What’s their.. work?”
	DENIZ: (stares blankly in silence for a few seconds)
	NARRATOR: This was, in fact, a stupid question, so this isn’t exactly a strange look to receive.
	Deniz: “..A ferryman.”
	<<set $DenizAnger1 = true>>
	<<set $BoatDenizAnger = $BoatDenizAnger + 1>>
	<<jump DenizQuests>>
-> “Uh.. Where do they live?” <<if $DenizAnger2 == false>>
	SASHA: “Uh.. Where do they live?”
	Deniz: (mutters) Sky district.
	<<set $DenizAnger2 = true>>
	<<set $BoatDenizAnger = $BoatDenizAnger + 1>>
	<<jump DenizQuests>>
-> “What’s their weird secret? They keep acting..”<<if $DenizAnger3 == false>>
	SASHA: “What’s their weird secret? They keep acting..”
	DENIZ: (shrugs)
	<<set $DenizAnger3 = true>>
	<<set $BoatDenizAnger = $BoatDenizAnger + 1>>
	<<jump DenizQuests>>
-> “...Wait, why are you so mad?”
	Sasha: “...Wait, why are you so mad?”
	<<if $BoatDenizAnger == 3>>
		DENIZ: (Silence)
		DENIZ: (Suddenly turns back to the water, visibly irritated)
		Deniz: (scoff) “What do you care? You’re probably just here on their request, anyway.”
		Deniz: “Tell them this: Shove it. I don’t want to talk to you anymore. Not now, not ever.”
		-> Are you sure that’s.. what you want me to say?
		-> No, I’m really not here because they..
		NARRATOR: Whatever it is you’re saying, they’re pointedly looking away from you, not giving a single flying fuck. Even the dog stops panting behind them- her big round eyes set on you in a curious, albeit unsure manner.
		NARRATOR: Perhaps this situation is a little more tender than you’d thought. 
		<<set $BoatSashaAnger = true>>
		<<stop>>
	<<endif>>
	<<jump ContDeniz>>
===
title: ContDeniz
---
Deniz: (after a moment of silence) “And what do you care?”
-> "Just.. curious"
	<<stop>>
-> "What's going on between you two?"
Sasha: "What's going on between you two?"
DENIZ: (scoffs) “That's none of your business, and even if it was..” (trail off, beat of silence)
DENIZ: “It doesn't matter anymore. Not now, anyway.”
-> Deniz, I've just watched the world end, and I'm back to see everything again as a sort of groundhog day. Please, for the love of god, indulge me.
-> What if I said please?
DENIZ: (silence)
DOG: (panting behind DENIZ, walks over to sniff SASHA's leg)

-> What's the dog's name?
	Deniz: “Lexa.”
-> Deniz.. please.
Deniz: (sigh)“Look.. I really don't want to talk about it alright? It's.. petty. And stupid.”
<<if $PsychMajor == true>>
PSY: There's a tremor in their tone.
<<endif>>
Deniz: “Look, I don't even care if Boat sent you anymore. Tell them this: not today. They should be doing their job, and me.. I should be.. staying far away from this nonsense.”
<<Learn DenizBoatHate>> 
-> "Are you not religious?"
	Sasha: "Are you not religious?"
	DENIZ: (uncomfortable silence)
		-> "It's okay, me neither."
			Sasha: "It's okay, me neither."
			<<jump ReligionDeniz>>
		-> "You're safe to tell me."
			Sasha: "You're safe to tell me."
			<<jump ReligionDeniz>>
		-> "Booooo."
				Sasha: "Booooo."
-> "Alright, well.. thank you for telling me."

<<set $IslandQuestDenizUnfinished = false>>
<<stop>>
===
title: ReligionDeniz
---
Deniz: (hesitant) "I'm not.. religious, I guess. It's never been something I found interesting, in fact.."
Deniz: "I think it's ridiculous, all of this. A whole waste of time and energy and- and frankly, I don't know why everyone likes it so much."
Deniz: "I really thought the only man who was worth my time with his whole religion thing was Alfonz, but he's.. well.. gone."
Deniz: (slowly shakes head) "And it's not like he could convince me or anything like that."
Deniz: "Alfonz was just..."
Deniz: "Kind."
-> "I understand. Alfonz was like my father."
	NARRATOR: Your voice broke, how embarrassing.
	Deniz: "Oh.. I'm sorry to hear that."
-> That's unfortunate.
	DENIZ: (nods, turns to the dog by their side.)

DENIZ: (After some silence) "What's.. what's your name? I guess I forgot to ask.."
-> "Sasha."
	Sasha: "Sasha."
	<<set $DenizKnowsSasha = true>>
	DENIZ: (nods slowly, finally meets SASHA's eyes for the first time)
	Deniz: "Sasha.. Okay, I'll try to remember that."
-> "None of your business."
	Sasha: "None of your business."
	Deniz: "..Huh?"
	Deniz: (uncomfortable) "..Well, alright."
<<set $IslandQuestDenizUnfinished = false>>
(DENIZ leans back onto their hands, THE DOG crawls on their lap.)
DENIZ: I'm uh.. sure you have better places to be than here. Goodbye.
NARRATOR: They're probably right in that. Time's ticking.

